You have post concussion vision syndrome. This means that after a head injury, the visual system is not working as efficiently as before. This can lead to a variety of symptoms including light sensitivity, blurred vision, eye strain, difficulty focusing, double vision, headaches, trouble with reading and screen use, and a sense of dizziness or problems with balance.  \
\
These symptoms are common after concussion and usually improve over time as the brain recovers.\
\
